  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "Reimagined as a nourishing morning meal, this Greek <b>egg-lemon breakfast soup</b> offers silky comfort and bright citrus wake-up energy. Rich chicken stock is simmered with soft short-grain rice and fragrant oregano before being thickened with tempered egg yolks and lemon juice. Soft-boiled poached eggs rest in each bowl, releasing velvety yolk into the velvety citrus broth when broken. Crushed barley rusks add hearty whole-grain texture that softens pleasantly into the soup. Fresh dill, crumbled feta cheese, and cracked black pepper top each portion for layers of savory herbal contrast. Designed to start the day with warm vitality, this dish combines traditional Mediterranean citrus soup with breakfast elements like eggs and whole grains. Light yet deeply satisfying, it brings sunny Greek flavors to the breakfast table in a quick half-hour preparation.",
